.TH KAERU 1 "2026-11-16" "kaeru 0.2.0" "Kaeru manual"
.SH NAME
kaeru \- keep your computer awake on request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kaeru
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Kaeru
asks the desktop to prevent automatic system sleep and screen blanking
(via the xdg\-desktop\-portal Inhibit interface, with a systemd\-logind
sleep:block fallback). Keep Awake can run for 15 minutes, 30 minutes,
1 hour, 2 hours, or until turned off. Choosing a new duration replaces the
current request; requests never stack.
.PP
Kaeru never modifies global power\-management settings and never
synthesizes input activity. Everything is local: no accounts, no cloud and
no telemetry. The Focus Timer, Work Log and Reports features are deferred
from this release; their source and any existing stored data are preserved.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B (no command)
Open the application window.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start without showing the window (tray only).
.TP
.B \-\-awake\-on\-login
Start hidden and enable Keep Awake indefinitely. Used by the autostart
entry; combine with \fB\-\-background\fR.
.TP
.B status
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show the current Keep Awake status.
.TP
.B awake on
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fI30m\fR] [\fB\-\-mode\fR \fIsystem|display|both\fR]
Request Keep Awake for a duration. A new request replaces the current one.
.TP
.B awake indefinite
Keep awake until explicitly turned off.
.TP
.B awake off
Turn Keep Awake off now.
.TP
.B diagnostics
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show capability and backend diagnostics.
.TP
.B open
Show the window of a running Kaeru instance.
.TP
.B quit
Quit a running Kaeru instance, releasing inhibitors.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
ok
.TP
.B 2
usage error
.TP
.B 3
Kaeru not running
.TP
.B 4
failed
.TP
.B 5
permission denied
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kaeru/
Settings (kaeru.conf).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/kaeru/kaeru.db
Local database. Work Log storage is preserved for a future release; it is
not used by the user interface in this version.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/io.github.kaeru.Kaeru.desktop
Optional per-user autostart entry, created only when enabled in Settings.
